    {
      "sha": "6b9e0e375f704a01bef99f1a85924cebe048079b",
      "date": "2025-01-10T00:20:41Z",
      "author": "Lidiane Taquehara",
      "email": "lidi.mayra@gmail.com",
      "message": "Add Post representation using JPA\n\nJPA Entities are POJOs associated to data that can be persisted to\ndatabase. `Post` Entity represents a table of posts in the DB. Therefore\nan instance of a `Post` can be used to manage a row in this table.\n\nPostRepository it's an interface that extends JPARepository. By doing\nthat, it inherits different methods that can be used for common\npersistence operations.\n"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4244a06ff9a34f10e831d23c5d9e7522d581afb5",
